WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.636
-My first guest is an Emmy
and Golden Globe-winning actor

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:07.073
who you can see in the big new
film, "Godzilla vs. Kong,"

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.943
which is in theaters
and on HBO Max on March 31st.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.513
Please welcome
Alexander Skarsgard!

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.815
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.751
Ah, that's what --
that's what I'm talking about.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.252
Look at you, stud.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.355
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.423
It's been a while since
last you were on the show,

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:27.527
and I was reading that
you've been really dedicating

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:31.564
the past few months
to drawing and artwork.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.734
-Sounds kind of pretentious,
but in the beginning

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:39.072
of the lockdown a year ago,
I wanted to stay creative

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.808
and not just stare
into the wall.

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:46.278
-Yeah.
-So I started drawing.

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:49.816
And I hadn't done
much of that before.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:53.753
But I got really into it.
Went deep down the rabbit hole.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.822
In the beginning,
it was mostly like croquis stuff

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:59.258
and rough drawings,
but then --

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:01.861
-Croquis? Is that, like,
a style of drawing?

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.930
-Yeah.
Yeah, and it evolved into

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.432
more portrait mode
and more detailed drawing.

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:09.435
I got into the --
kind of the geometry behind it

00:01:09.435 --> 00:01:13.472
to get the proportions right,
and I've probably spent

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:17.577
a couple of thousand hours
now just drawing.

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:21.914
-Wow.
-It's like Malcolm Gladwell's

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.117
theory that --
Well, I don't know if --

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.552
10,000 hours you spend
on something.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.653
-Yeah, you become a master.

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.456
-I haven't reached
that level quite, but it's been,

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:33.425
you know, a good part
of the past year

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:36.196
just drawing portraits

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:39.632
and still life
and basically everything.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.735
-Do you have any drawings nearby
that you could maybe show us?

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.370
I'd love to see a couple.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.505
-Yeah.
Uh...

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.173
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.241
It's a bit embarrassing.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.442
I haven't shown
a lot of people this

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:54.013
'cause I've been so isolated,
but, um, yeah.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.414
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.414 --> 00:02:00.986
So...
this is...my mom's dog.

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:07.360
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.595
-Okay.
Wow.

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.964
-Yeah, that's my mom's dog.
-Amazing.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.300
-And when I drew it,
it was actually just standing.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.637
But I wanted it to be more
kinetic and have more life.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:18.804
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, of course!

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:21.774
So you added --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.610
'Cause the dog --
So, the dog was standing

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.646
when you saw it,
but yet you wanted to add

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.548
a little movement to it.
Yeah.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.016
-Creative freedom.
Creative freedom.

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:32.252
-No, no, absolutely.
That's what I meant to say.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.587
-Yeah. Congratulations.
Any others?

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.156
-Well, yeah.
Part of the training was also

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:42.962
kind of to draw reproductions
of the old classics.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:47.599
And so I have...

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.736
Michelangelo.
-Oh, of course.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.871
Okay, well...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.940
Okay. That's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.775
No, you're right.
That angle is correct.

00:02:56.775 --> 00:02:59.945
-And I -- basically,
when I drew this,

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:01.413
I don't even remember doing it.

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:04.417
Like, I put pen to paper,
and then I kind of zoned out,

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:08.587
and then --
-At what point do you zone out?

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:11.056
-Well, basically when I put
pen to paper on this one,

00:03:11.056 --> 00:03:12.458
I don't even remember
drawing it.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.994
And then I looked up,
and I was like, "Wow."

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:18.530
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.633
That's exactly what I would do.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.736
-I wasn't even religious
before I started doing this,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.537
But then I was like, I saw God.

00:03:25.537 --> 00:03:27.273
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my gosh.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.641
Yeah, of course.
-And I don't even know

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.810
if I did it or, like,
the hand of God --

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.114
it was drawn by the hand of God.
-Honestly, Alexander...

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:40.019
-And then I took a stab at
the most classic of them all,

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.823
the most classic masterpiece,
"Mona Lisa."

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.525
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:47.760
-Yeah, that's --
That's actually not bad.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.295
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.531
-I --
-It's not --

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:56.001
I'm not quite happy
with the enigmatic smile.

00:03:56.001 --> 00:03:57.569
I'm working on that.

00:03:57.569 --> 00:03:59.672
-Yeah, no, I think
you nailed it perfect.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.907
I have a lot of --
I have a lot of questions.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:03.509
I look at that, and I have
a lot of questions,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.877
just like the real work of art.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.946
-Do you really?
-Yep.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.180
-Thanks, man!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.449
-Yeah, congratulations.
Yeah.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:10.682
-Thank you, man.

00:04:10.682 --> 00:04:13.152
-Buddy, I always love
having you on the show.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.020
Congrats on "Godzilla vs. Kong."

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.556
'Cause people are saying
right now it's on track

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:22.361
to become the biggest box office
since the pandemic started.

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.696
And I'm excited about it.

00:04:24.696 --> 00:04:25.998
Can you set it up a little bit?

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:29.469
Like, why is Godzilla
fighting King Kong?

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:33.305
-Um...
Well, in the last

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:35.942
Godzilla movie,
that one is called

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.443
"Godzilla:
King of the Monsters,"

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:41.547
and the outcome is kind of
in the title.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.449
By the end of the movie,
he is the king.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:48.087
And he's the apex predator on
the planet, and everyone agrees.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:53.359
And then, in this movie,
Kong basically shows up.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:54.860
'Cause he wasn't in
"King of Monsters,"

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.030
and Kong is like,

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:02.568
"Hold my banana
while I spank this lizard."

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:03.802
-Yep.
Yep, yep, yep.

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:06.705
"Hold my banana while I
spank this lizard," yeah.

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.040
-That's not metaphorically --

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.276
-That was the original
tagline of the movie.

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:11.443
But they didn't use it.

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:13.012
But without giving away
spoilers,

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:14.913
Tariq and I have a bet.

00:05:14.913 --> 00:05:19.651
And Godzilla versus Kong,
you have to make a bet.

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:21.887
Do you have a preference?
Who are you betting on,

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:24.490
and did you have
a preference, like, growing up?

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.358
-Wait. So, Jimmy,
who did you bet on?

00:05:26.358 --> 00:05:28.360
-I bet on Kong.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.629
King Kong, by the way.

00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:33.732
-So, not me, basically.

00:05:33.732 --> 00:05:36.802
-Well, this is before
I talked to you.

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:38.170
-Right.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.907
It is Godzilla versus Kong
versus Alexander Skarsgard.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.741
-Yes! And that I would
take the bet.

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:43.876
-The great titan.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.945
-I would take
Alexander Skarsgard

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.880
all the time.
Every single time.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.148
That's the king.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:52.451
You're the king of all man!

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:53.919
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:56.155
Here's King Kong
fighting off Godzilla

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:59.859
in "Godzilla vs. Kong."
Take a look at this.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:07.200
♪♪

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.869
[ Roaring ]

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.170
[ Screaming ]

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.905
[ Roaring ]

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:19.779
♪♪

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:26.652
♪♪

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.321
Yo!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:31.456
That is what I'm talking about,
buddy.

00:06:31.456 --> 00:06:33.493
I love it. Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:35.227
Every single time,
you're one of my faves.

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:37.796
Alexander Skarsgard, everybody.
-Ah, thank you.

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:40.666
-"Godzilla vs. Kong"
is in theaters

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:43.403
and streaming on HBO Max,
starting March 31st.

